{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneLRModulusFold"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.block_dims_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.block_dims_explicit","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L89-L97","doc":"The four block dimensions as an explicit Chebyshev tuple in `t` — the\ncontinuation object: evaluate at `t = φ` for the (folded) root data, at\n`t = q₀+q₀⁻¹` for the physical q₀ data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.wlambda_ratio_is_qi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.wlambda_ratio_is_qi","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L80-L87","doc":"**The continuation is evaluation.** The four block quantum dimensions are fixed\n`qi` polynomials in `t`; therefore any W_λ ratio (in which the `D²` normaliser\ncancels) is a ratio of `qi` polynomials — the root value and the archimedean `q₀`\nvalue are that one rational function at `t = φ` versus `t = q₀ + q₀⁻¹`.  Stated for\nthe electron/muon ratio numerator: `d((3,1,1)) − d((3,2)) = 1` for all `t`, an\nidentity of polynomials, hence continuation-stable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.electron_muon_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.electron_muon_split","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L75-L78","doc":"**The electron/muon split**: `d((3,1,1)) = d((3,2)) + 1` — the archimedean\ncontinuation carries the `+1` split signature at every `t`, so the electron block\nnever coincides with the muon block off the trivial locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.muon_unfolds_generic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.muon_unfolds_generic","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L68-L73","doc":"**The muon block unfolds off the fold**: the *same* quantum-dimension is the\npolynomial `d((3,2))(t) = t⁴ − 3t² + 1`, non-trivial for generic `t`.  Evaluated at\nthe substrate `t = q₀ + q₀⁻¹` this is the physical `[5]_{q₀} ≈ 5.22`, not `0` — the\narchimedean continuation unfolds the root degeneracy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.muon_folds_at_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.muon_folds_at_root","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L62-L66","doc":"**The muon block folds to zero at the fibre root** `t = φ` (`φ² = φ + 1`,\n`φ = 2cos(π/5)`): `d((3,2))(φ) = [5]_φ = 0`.  This is the `D = 2` degeneracy of the\nroot-of-unity fibre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.dq311","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.dq311","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L58-L60","doc":"Quantum dimension of the electron block `(3,1,1)`: `d = [5] + 1` (the A₅-split\n`3 ⊕ 3′` signature; equivalently `[3][4]/[2]`, `KeystoneMcKayValueMap`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.dq32","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.dq32","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L55-L56","doc":"Quantum dimension of the muon block `(3,2)`: `d = [5]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.dq41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.dq41","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L52-L53","doc":"Quantum dimension of the block `(4,1)`: `d = [4]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.dqVac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.dqVac","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneWLambdaContinuation.lean#L49-L50","doc":"Quantum dimension of the vacuum block `(5)`: `d = [1] = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}